  "prompt": "Product: BlueCat. Demo: \"Manage Overlapping Subnets Across Meraki Networks\".\nStory: Overlapping Subnets Across Meraki Sites, Without Guesswork\nBranch templates reuse the same subnets at every office. Watch BlueCat Micetro show each overlapping instance, let you separate one site to manage on its own, and bring it back. About 5 minutes.\nAudience: network and DNS engineers and IT leaders evaluating the product. Tone: concise, confident, practical, no hype.\n34 screenshots, keep this order, one tooltip per image, calling out the highlighted UI element:\n1. Your branch template reuses the same subnets at every office.\n2. Switch to the flat view.\n3. Four offices reuse the same guest subnet. Micetro shows every instance in one place, so nothing is guessed.\n4. Hover a row and its menu button appears.\n5. Open the row menu for the overlapping range.\n6. Opening an overlapping range adds an instance selector.\n7. Each instance is a Meraki network. The selector names every one.\n8. This is Oslo's guest network: its reservations, its clients.\n9. Open the selector again.\n10. Same CIDR, different reality. Switch instance and the data switches with it.\n11. Back to the network list.\n12. Flat view again.\n13. Find the range again.\n14. Hover the row to bring up its menu again.\n15. Open the row menu.\n16. You decide, not the software: isolate one site to manage it on its own.\n17. Start from none selected.\n18. Pick Oslo.\n19. Pick Helsinki.\n20. Separate the two instances.\n21. Add a change comment.\n22. A separated instance has its own range, its own IPs, its own custom properties.\n23. Hover the separated Oslo row.\n24. Open the menu on the separated Oslo instance.\n25. Reintegrate and the instance returns to the shared range. A Title set on a separated row is lost, as documented.\n26. Reintegrate Oslo.\n27. Add a change comment.\n28. Oslo is back in the shared range.\n29. Hover the separated Helsinki row.\n30. Now the Helsinki instance.\n31. Reintegrate it too.\n32. Confirm.\n33. Add a change comment.\n34. Back to one range with all four instances.\nClose: Overlaps are shown, never guessed: you choose which instances to isolate and which to keep together.\nEnd with a call to action: Bring your branch templates to a Micetro evaluation.",
